{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ae4c2bX2JtwP2ixMJ9XFf8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Product document for `fix-loop-own-words`.\n2\t#\n3\t# The catalogue phrases every step of E2E-001 but its last; the fix adds\n4\t# the entry that phrases \"the service answers within 200 milliseconds\",\n5\t# its meaning as the person put it in their own words.\n6\t\n7\ttitle: \"Fixture host project\"\n8\t\n9\tdescription:\n10\t  summary: >-\n11\t    A single MCP service, used by the bdd-cli fixtures as the host\n12\t    project a scenario registry describes.\n13\t\n14\troles:\n15\t  - name: Operator\n16\t    definition: Runs the MCP service and watches what it answers.\n17\t  - name: Client Developer\n18\t    definition: Writes the clients that send the MCP service its requests.\n19\t\n20\tglossary:\n21\t  - term: mcp service\n22\t    means: >-\n23\t      The service this project builds: it takes a message from a client\n24\t      and answers it. What every Scenario of the project observes.\n25\t  - term: reply\n26\t    means: >-\n27\t      What the MCP service sends back for one message, and how long it\n28\t      took to arrive. A client waits on it, so its content and its delay\n29\t      are both behaviour.\n30\t\n31\tcatalogue:\n32\t  - template: 'the mcp service is running'\n33\t    block: given\n34\t    means: The MCP service has started and accepts requests.\n35\t    terms: [mcp service]\n36\t  - template: 'the {actor:role} sends \"{message}\"'\n37\t    block: when\n38\t    means: That role sends the quoted message to the MCP service, once.\n39\t    terms: [mcp service]\n40\t  - template: 'the service answers \"{reply}\"'\n41\t    block: then\n42\t    means: The MCP service's reply to the message is exactly the quoted text.\n43\t    terms: [mcp service, reply]\n44\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9ba7005e-5e0d-43ae-a6f0-e18d81b9d17f","uuid":"2b644339-7d46-4ce0-a1dc-1e10fa01abf5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:36:3